---
/** The story. Warm, short, no manifesto. docs/05-website.md §8. */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Dictionary from '../components/Dictionary.astro';
import Circles from '../components/Circles.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { allTools } from '../lib/notes';

const tools = await allTools();
const loop = tools.find((t) => t.id === 'loop');
const cheri = tools.find((t) => t.id === 'cheri');
---

<Base
	title="Story"
	description="Why OPUS exists, what the name means, the three circles the tools serve, and how the studio stays alive."
	path="/story/"
	current="story"
>
	<article class="wrap wrap--narrow story">
		<header class="story__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">Story</p>
			<h1 class="voice">{SITE.thesis}</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				OPUS is a small studio in Cluj-Napoca. We make a few tools, slowly, for the parts of life that deserve
				care. Each one starts with a real need, gets made until it is complete, and is then left to do its job
				quietly.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="story__section">
			<h2 class="voice">The name</h2>
			<Dictionary size="large" />
			<p>Both are meant. The work, done the other way round.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="story__section">
			<h2 class="voice">Three circles</h2>
			<Circles
				rings={[
					{ label: loop?.data.name ?? 'Loop', circle: 'you with yourself', accent: loop?.data.accent },
					{ label: cheri?.data.name ?? 'Chéri', circle: 'you with your people', accent: cheri?.data.accent },
					{ label: 'the city', circle: 'you with everyone', dashed: true },
				]}
			/>
			<ul class="story__circles">
				<li><strong>Loop</strong> is for you with yourself: time, sound, silence.</li>
				<li><strong>Chéri</strong> is for you with your people: friends, and the things between them.</li>
				<li>A third tool, about the city, is in the works.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="story__section">
			<h2 class="voice">Where it comes from</h2>
			<p>
				For nearly two decades the founder designed mobile products for other companies. In 2026 OPUS made its
				first tool of its own, and the studio stopped being a plan. Every tool since has come from something we
				needed and could not find made the way we wanted it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="story__section">
			<h2 class="voice">How it stays alive</h2>
			<p>
				Loop is free with one preset, and a small price once for as many as you like. Chéri will be paid for
				once. Nothing we make asks you for money every month, and nothing we make needs an account.
			</p>
			<p>
				The studio is kept going by the people who find the work valuable, and by design work we do for a small
				number of startups. <a href="/support/">Here is how supporting it works</a>, and <a href="/work/">here
				is how we work with others</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="story__section">
			<h2 class="voice">Who</h2>
			<p>
				OPUS is C., a designer with nearly twenty years of mobile work behind him, and the people he makes
				things with. It is {SITE.legal} on paper.
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</Base>

<style>
	.story {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-2xl);
	}
	.story__head {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-m);
	}
	.story__section {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-m);
	}
	.story__section p,
	.story__circles {
		font-size: var(--step-0);
		color: var(--ink);
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	.story__circles {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-2xs);
	}
	.story__circles strong {
		font-weight: 600;
	}
</style>
